      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1913 the town already had stores, schools, churches, a bank, a doctor’s office, and a newspaper, thanks to railroad lines from Visalia Electric and Santa Fe.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
