      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city sits in the San Joaquin Valley about 22 miles east of Visalia, nestled at the base of the Sierra Nevada foothills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Woodlake,_California",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Woodlake’s economy is driven by citrus, olive, and dairy farming, making it a key player in California’s citrus belt.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Woodlake,_California",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Outdoor lovers can fish and hike near Bravo Lake or head to Sequoia and Kings Canyon National Parks, both within easy reach.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
